":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9.2 x 6.3 x 1.4 inches","oclc_numbers":["842680848","42289672","51494045"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Reconstructing Manichaeism from scraps of ancient texts and the ungenerous polemic of its enemies (such as the ex-Manichaean Augustine of Hippo), BeDuhn reveals for the first time the religion as it was actually practiced. He describes the Manichaeans' daily ritual meal, their stringent disciplinary codes (intended to prevent humans from harming plants and animals), and their surprising religious procedures designed to transform the cosmos and bring about the salvation of all living beings.\".\n\n\"BeDuhn's conclusions revolutionize our understanding of the Manichaeans, clearly distinguishing them from Gnostics and other early Christian heretics and revealing them to be practitioners of a unique world religion.\n\nAlong the way, he argues for the priority of practice over doctrine in determining religious identity, raises central questions about the modern methods of studying religions, and proposes ways to address the challenge of conveying ancient and alien realities to the modern world.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":19,"revision":19,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T15:03:11.581851"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-01T00:55:17.943073"}}},"ISBN:9780801874611":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780801874611","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL36698166M/Manichaean_Body","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL36698166M/Manichaean_Body","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2799305A","name":"Jason David BeDuhn"}],"isbn_13":["9780801874611"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["BT1410.B43 2000"],"pagination":"376","publish_date":"2003","publishers":["Johns Hopkins University Press"],"source_records":["bwb:9780801874611"],"subjects":["Manichaeism"],"title":"Manichaean Body","subtitle